Lab 3: OpenStack Service Components Overview
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will:

Understand the core OpenStack services (Keystone, Glance, Nova, Neutron, Cinder) and their roles.
Configure and verify basic functionality of each service.
Analyze service interactions and dependencies.
Monitor service status and troubleshoot common issues.
Prerequisites
A working OpenStack deployment (DevStack or manual installation).
Administrative access to the OpenStack controller node.
Basic Linux command-line proficiency.
Python 3.x installed (for API interactions).
Lab Setup
Access the OpenStack Controller Node
SSH into your OpenStack controller node:

ssh <username>@<controller-ip_address>
Verify OpenStack Services
Ensure the OpenStack services are running:

sudo systemctl list-units "openstack-*" --no-pager
Expected Output: Active (running) status for core services.

Task 1: Configure and Verify OpenStack Services
Subtask 1.1: Keystone (Identity Service)
Objective: Set up and test Keystone for authentication.

Create a Service Project:

openstack project create --domain default --description "Service Project" service
Verify Keystone Endpoints:

openstack catalog list
Expected Output: List of registered services (e.g., identity, compute, image).

Create a Demo User and Role:

openstack user create --domain default --password-prompt demo
openstack role create user
openstack role add --project demo --user demo user
Troubleshooting: If errors occur, check /var/log/keystone/keystone.log.

Subtask 1.2: Glance (Image Service)
Objective: Upload and manage a VM image.

Download a Test Image:

wget https://download.cirros-cloud.net/0.6.1/cirros-0.6.1-x86_64-disk.img
Upload to Glance:

openstack image create "cirros" --file cirros-0.6.1-x86_64-disk.img \
--disk-format qcow2 --container-format bare --public
Verify Image:

openstack image list
Expected Output: cirros image listed as active.

Subtask 1.3: Nova (Compute Service)
Objective: Launch an instance using Nova.

Create a Flavor:

openstack flavor create --ram 512 --disk 1 --vcpus 1 m1.tiny
Launch an Instance:

openstack server create --image cirros --flavor m1.tiny --network demo-net demo-instance
Check Instance Status:

openstack server list
Expected Output: demo-instance in ACTIVE state.

Subtask 1.4: Neutron (Networking Service)
Objective: Configure a network and subnet.

Create a Network:

openstack network create demo-net
Create a Subnet:

openstack subnet create --network demo-net --subnet-range 192.168.1.0/24 demo-subnet
Verify Network:

openstack network list
Expected Output: demo-net listed with UP status.

Subtask 1.5: Cinder (Block Storage Service)
Objective: Create and attach a volume.

Create a 1GB Volume:

openstack volume create --size 1 demo-volume
Attach to Instance:

openstack server add volume demo-instance demo-volume
Verify Attachment:

openstack volume show demo-volume
Expected Output: status as in-use.

Task 2: Service Interactions and Dependencies
Subtask 2.1: Trace API Calls
Enable Debug Logging: Edit /etc/nova/nova.conf:

[DEFAULT]
debug = True
Restart Nova Services:

sudo systemctl restart openstack-nova-*
Check Logs:

tail -f /var/log/nova/nova-api.log
Key Concept: Observe Keystone authentication before Nova actions.

Task 3: Monitoring and Troubleshooting
Subtask 3.1: Check Service Status
List All Services:

openstack compute service list
openstack network agent list
Debug a Failed Service:

sudo journalctl -u openstack-nova-compute --no-pager -n 50
Conclusion
In this lab, you:

Configured and validated core OpenStack services (Keystone, Glance, Nova, Neutron, Cinder).
Explored service dependencies through API interactions.
Monitored services and practiced troubleshooting.
